<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Snow Creek Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:256-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.160159" lon="-121.636767"><ele>1572.2</ele><name>Upper Three Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 100326940); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 5120; quote: map 58: UPPER 3 CREEK SNO-PARK 5120'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.117400" lon="-121.628480"><ele>1933.0</ele><name>Snow Creek Trail leaves Road 16 near Trapper Meadow</name><desc>source: USFS trail 4107 SNOW CREEK XC BMP 0.0 = Park Meadow 4075 BMP 0.0 (60 m south of the neighbours' Trapper Meadow point); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 6300; quote: starting near Trapper Meadow (also known as Three Creek Meadow). It follows the summer Park Meadow Trail, at first an old road. It leaves Road 16</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.122170" lon="-121.646970"><ele>1935.8</ele><name>Pumice desert</name><desc>source: 1.1 mi along USFS 4107 (shared with Park Meadow 4075); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 258; quote: following the mostly level, primitive road to a pumice desert at 1.1 miles</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.125590" lon="-121.660330"><ele>1880.7</ele><name>Right turn at Snow Creek</name><desc>source: where USFS 4107 leaves Park Meadow 4075 (Park Meadow Tie 4102 end), 2.0 mi along 4107; confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; quote: then descends steeply on a forest trail 0.8 mile to a right turn at Snow Creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.146860" lon="-121.652710"><ele>1717.2</ele><name>Snow Creek Trail meets Nancy's Loop</name><desc>source: end of USFS 4107 (EMP 4.0), 6 m from Nancy's Loop 4087; confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; quote: descends northward on moderate grades through beautiful, scattered meadows in a narrow valley, climbs a short ridge with ponderosas, and descends along the west legs of both Warren's and Nancy's Loops</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.149420" lon="-121.649360"><ele>1695.6</ele><name>Nancy's Loop meets Warren's Loop</name><desc>source: end of USFS 4086 WARREN'S XC (EMP 0.96), on Nancy's Loop 4087 (2 m); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; quote: descends along the west legs of both Warren's and Nancy's Loops</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.153620" lon="-121.636240"><ele>1667.7</ele><name>Warren's Loop meets Three Creek Trail</name><desc>source: USFS 4084 BMP 0.7 = 4086 BMP 0.0; confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; quote: From the sno-park ski up the Three Creek Trial 0.7 mile to Warren's Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.160240" lon="-121.638620"><ele>1576.0</ele><name>Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16</name><desc>source: USFS trail 4084 THREE CREEKS LAKE XC, BMP 0.0 (on OSM NF 16 node 38583495, 5 m); confidence: high; pdf_page: 257; quote: From the sno-park ski a few yards south up Road 16 past the gate and turn right onto the Three Creek Lake Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.160159" lon="-121.636767"><ele>1572.2</ele><name>Upper Three Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 100326940); confidence: high; pdf_page: 258; book_elev_ft: 5120; quote: map 58: UPPER 3 CREEK SNO-PARK 5120'</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Snow Creek Trail</name><desc>1. Upper Three Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Snow Creek Trail leaves Road 16 near Trapper Meadow: osm (high), 3.52 mi | 2. Snow Creek Trail leaves Road 16 near Trapper Meadow -&gt; Pumice desert: usfs-trail (high), 1.10 mi | 3. Pumice desert -&gt; Right turn at Snow Creek: usfs-trail (high), 0.99 mi | 4. Right turn at Snow Creek -&gt; Snow Creek Trail meets Nancy's Loop: usfs-trail (high), 1.80 mi | 5. Snow Creek Trail meets Nancy's Loop -&gt; Nancy's Loop meets Warren's Loop: usfs-trail (high), 0.25 mi | 6. Nancy's Loop meets Warren's Loop -&gt; Warren's Loop meets Three Creek Trail: usfs-trail (high), 0.98 mi | 7. Warren's Loop meets Three Creek Trail -&gt; Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16: usfs-trail (high), 0.71 mi | 8. Three Creek Lake Trail leaves Road 16 -&gt; Upper Three Creek Sno-Park: osm (high), 0.11 mi</desc>
